{"Title":"An Act relative to embarkation fees","BillNumber":"S3016","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S30","Name":"Senate Committee on Ways and Means","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S30","ResponseDate":"2024-12-30T12:08:46.153"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-15T22:49:48.52"},{"Id":"KAD1","Name":"Kip A. Diggs","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:34:42.2866667"},{"Id":"SLM0","Name":"Susan L. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLM0","ResponseDate":"2023-03-30T13:38:45.8466667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S3016/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"Senate, December 30, 2024 -- The committee on Senate Ways and Means, to whom was referred the Senate Bill relative to embarkation fees (Senate, No. 2873),- reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment substituting a new draft with the same title (Senate, No. 3016).","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 129 of Chapter 46 of the acts of 2003, as amended by Section 11 of Chapter 55 of the acts of 2003, is hereby amended by striking out the figure “$.50”, each time it appears, and inserting in place thereof the following figure:- $1.00.\r\n\t SECTION 2. Any city or town who has previously accepted section 129 of Chapter 46 of the acts of 2003, as amended by Section 11 of Chapter 55 of the acts of 2003, may continue to impose previously approved embarkation fees of $.50 per passenger per departing trip. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}